algovoi-fabric is a composition core: it binds independently published
protocols into one tamper-evident, offline-verifiable journey and claims
nothing over any of them. It reuses their own verifiers rather than
re-implementing cryptography or canonicalisation:

  * AV-RAILS / algovoi-keystone and algovoi-keystone-connect, by AlgoVoi
    (Apache-2.0): the decision chain and the canonical keystone_ref primitive.
  * AV-PEF / algovoi-pef, by AlgoVoi (Apache-2.0): payment evidence frames.
  * AV-VCS / algovoi-substrate, by AlgoVoi (Apache-2.0): sealed-archive bindings.
  * avm-ac2 and avm-mesh, by AlgoVoi (Apache-2.0): AC2 settlement consent and
    the sealed receipt format. AC2 (Agentic Communication and Control) is a
    Draft specification published by the Algorand Foundation at
    https://github.com/algorandfoundation/ac2; no AC2 code is bundled here.
  * rfc8785 (Apache-2.0): JSON Canonicalization Scheme.

